        </h1>
        <h1>THE UNSEEN BEAUTY</h1>
        <p>Where Mountains Meet The Sea</p>
        <h2>Why Balochistan</h2>
        <p>Pakistan's largest province, but least explored. It has everything in one place-golden desert, blue beaches, snowy forests, volcanoes, and 7000 years of history. Row, peaceful, and untouched. No crowd, no noise-just nature.</p>
        <h3>Places you must visit</h3>
        <h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Kun Malir Beach-Gwadar Coastal Highway</li>
        </ol>
        </h3>
        <p>Golden desert mountains touching blue sea. This is not Maldives, this is better and it's <br>ours. Camp at night, stars look like diamonds. Best time:<br>October to March</p>
        <h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Hingol National Park-Pakistan's Largest</li>
        </ol>
        </h3>
        <p>Feels like Mars on Earth. You will see Princess of Hope (naturak rock statue), Active mud volcanoes, and wild ibex. Also home to Hinglaj Mata Temple. Jeep safari is a must.</p> 
        <h3>
            <ol>
                <li>Ziarat-City of Juniper (Near Quetta)</li>
            </ol>
        </h3>
        <p>5000-year-old juniper forests-some are the oldest trees in the world. Quid-e-Azam <br>Residency, snowfall in winter, and pure peace.Best for family trip from Quetta</p>
